\ A task that borrows the load lock from a holder awaiting it can reach the very module that
\ holder is still loading. That is a re-entrant load, and it reports as one rather than recursing.
\ `use` runs at parse time and cannot be caught, so each case reaches the loader through the
\ runtime `load` word.

use "testing" ;

"delegated re-entry into an in-flight load" test-section

\ One load, so the outer module's start marker below appears exactly once and its end marker not
\ at all: the re-entry is rejected instead of running the top level a second time.
[ "fixtures/reentry_outer.1z" load ] [ ] recover

dup error-type: @get
load-in-flight: "a delegated re-entry is not reported as a cycle" assert=

\ Task 1 is the scope task `task-scope` runs the outer module's body in, so task 2 is the loader
\ spawned inside it.
message: @get
"load in flight: ./reentry_outer.1z is loading on main, re-entered on task[2]: fixtures/reentry_outer.1z -> ./reentry_inner.1z -> ./reentry_outer.1z"
"the message names the module, both owners, and the chain" assert=

"an ordinary cycle through a task-scope" test-section

\ Nothing is spawned here. The scope still runs its body in its own task, so the re-entry arrives
\ under a different owner and reports as a re-entrant load. The chain is what a reader needs, and
\ it is named either way.
\
\ Task ids count from 1 per worker pool and a top-level `task-scope` builds its own, so the scope
\ task is task 1 again here.
[ "fixtures/reentry_scope_outer.1z" load ] [ ] recover

dup error-type: @get
load-in-flight: "a cycle whose middle load sits in a scope reads as a re-entry" assert=

message: @get
"load in flight: ./reentry_scope_outer.1z is loading on main, re-entered on task[1]: fixtures/reentry_scope_outer.1z -> ./reentry_scope_a.1z -> ./reentry_scope_outer.1z"
"the chain names the module the cycle passed through" assert=

"a cycle on the borrowing task is still a cycle" test-section

\ The borrower's own imports close a cycle, so both ends of it carry the borrower's identity and
\ the split must not fire merely because a hold was borrowed.
[ "fixtures/reentry_cycle_outer.1z" load ]
circular-dependency: "the borrower's own cycle keeps the cycle diagnostic" assert-error-type
